  "term": "spatial ability",
  "definition": "Spatial ability is a basic cognitive skill involved in understanding and working with spatial information, and it strongly predicts success in STEM learning. In this context, three-dimensional geometric thinking is a formalized use of spatial ability for solving three-dimensional geometry problems.",
